INT. MOBILE FIELD HOSPITAL TENT, FLOOD ZONE - NIGHT

Canvas walls snapping in wind. Generators outside. Cots in rows. Bags of IV fluid hang from tent poles. Mud on every surface.

DR. AMARACHI NWOSU-BELLINGHAM (40s, surgeon, scrubs under a poncho) kneels over a cot where a boy lies unconscious. NURSE FELIPE ARRIAGA-TOMLINSON (30s, glasses fogged, stethoscope slipping) squeezes a bag-valve mask. A volunteer, TESS KOWALEWSKI-AMADI (20s, Red Cross vest, hands shaking), holds a flashlight. A radio on a crate squawks.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio, static)
Field Two, Dispatch. Evacuation convoy is delayed. Repeat, convoy delayed. Estimate ninety minutes.

AMARACHI
Tess, hold the light steady.

TESS
I'm trying.

AMARACHI
Try harder.

Felipe squeezes the bag. The boy's chest rises. Falls. Amarachi puts two fingers to the boy's throat, and her face closes. She looks at Felipe. He sees it. His squeezing slows, then resumes, faster.

FELIPE
Doctor, we have a rhythm.

AMARACHI
We don't.

FELIPE
We have a pulse.

AMARACHI
We have a monitor reading its own noise.

Tess lowers the flashlight; Amarachi grabs her wrist and raises it again. Felipe bends over the boy and begins compressions, counting under his breath. The radio squawks. Tess jumps. The light swings across the tent roof, over the rows of cots, over a woman in the corner who has turned to watch.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Field Two, confirm receipt.

TESS
(whispering)
Should I answer?

AMARACHI
(without looking)
Answer.

Tess scrambles to the radio, still holding the flashlight, and keys the mic with her elbow.

TESS
(into radio)
Dispatch, Field Two. Copy. Ninety minutes.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Field Two, how many critical?

Tess looks at the boy. At Felipe, pumping the small chest. At Amarachi, her fingers still on the throat.

TESS
(into radio)
One. Maybe zero.

Amarachi sits back on her heels. Felipe stops compressions. He wipes his glasses on his sleeve, puts them back, and looks at her.

FELIPE
Time?

AMARACHI
Eleven forty-one.

FELIPE
I'll write it down.

AMARACHI
I'll write it.

She stands, steadies herself on a pole, and crosses to the radio. Takes the mic from Tess, who gives it up like a hot pan.

AMARACHI (CONT'D)
(into radio)
Dispatch, Field Two. Patient expired. Eleven forty-one. Send the convoy anyway. We have eleven more.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Copy, Field Two. We're sending it.

She sets the mic down very gently on the crate. Tess hands her a clipboard. Her hand is steady now.
